(
    version: 1,
    note: Some("The policy layer for site_v2, the Site's next kit. EMPTY ON PURPOSE, and it has to be: `Project::open` refuses a patch that matches no descriptor -- a rule that silently applies to nothing is how a policy rots -- so a kit with no library can carry no patches, and adding one before the pieces exist makes the editor unstartable. The ARCHITECTURE the site patches encode is a fact about the building rather than about any mesh, and belongs here once the pieces are imported and their ids are known: walls are built to 2.40 m and doorways to 2.00 m in this facility. assets/emerge/site/project.ron carries the shipped version of exactly those 8 patches and is the thing to read across from."),
    // How finely each authoring tile divides, for every piece's lattice. 1 means a subunit is
    // `grid::SNAP` itself -- the half-metre grid these kits are already authored on, on which a
    // 3 m wall is 6 divisions across and a 2.4 m one is 5 layers tall. Raising it refines every
    // piece in the project by the same factor, which is what keeps two faces comparable.
    face_bands: 1,
)
